SUMMARY:Knock\, Knock (Theatre for the Very Young)
DESCRIPTION:Knock\, Knock  is the perfect way to kick off the holiday season with this adventure through an apartment building.  Meet the various residents behind different doors and on different floors and see delivery boxes become imaginative forts\, snowflake crafting causing frustrations\, join a festive party\, and try to keep warm in the winter chill. \nThere are giggles and surprises behind every door\, and lots of chances to get involved with the action. \nCreated by Olivia Aston Bosworth and Samantha Provenzano \nCommissioned by Alliance Theatre \nOriginally developed and produced by the Alliance Theatre (Atlanta\, GA) as part of the Kathy and Ken Bernhardt Theatre for the Very Young series. \nSound Elements and Composition by Multiband Studios. \nDialogue complexity: no typical conversations\, performers use key words that are frequently repeated and rely on physical actions and props to tell the story. \n 
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/knock-knock-theatre-for-the-very-young/2026-11-22/1/
LOCATION:Raleigh Little Theatre\, 301 Pogue St\, Raleigh\, 27607
ORGANIZER;CN="Raleigh Little Theatre":MAILTO:boxoffice@raleighlittletheatre.org
END:VEVENT
